{"ts":"2026-08-28T14:54:28.347Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"7405dc9b453c8154184ac8fe","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-web-25nv"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The per-IP rate limiter trusted a client-supplied forwarded address by default, so any caller could rotate a header to a fresh bucket"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"resolveTrustProxy returned one trusted hop when PM_WEB_TRUST_PROXY was unset. Every launch path this package documents exposes Express directly with no proxy: a docker run publishing the port, and npm start. Under that default Express takes the client address from the caller's own X-Forwarded-For header, so an attacker rotating the header draws a new bucket for every request and every per-route limit added by this change enforces nothing, while still reporting itself as enforcing them. The default is now to trust nothing, which fails in the visible direction instead: a genuinely proxied deployment sees all clients share the proxy address and an operator notices immediately. The hosted deployment behind Caddy declares its single hop explicitly in the compose file, and the variable is documented."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:http","area:security","type:defect"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-28T14:54:28.347Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-28T14:54:28.347Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"2b45a6c7e35ef0525b35d749ac1b3b7ed1bd4e81c712ecb47ededb0305ba8fdd","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
